(6091446, 894640, 88850, '<td valign="top"><u></u></td>', '', '2010-07-13 19:46:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091541, 896261, 10785, '<td valign="top">I could see this being a really fun shot! The trick to making this pop is to make the game pop and capture the pieces flying around on camera, either in stop action or with motion blur! (Would that be chaos instead??) A few things to pick up on, and these are just somewhat minor, would be to get the camera directly overhead of the game to avoid the perspective lines... Also some color would add a bit more to the image! You are definitely thinking outside the box!</td>', 'I could see this being a really fun shot! The trick to making this pop is to make the game pop and capture the pieces flying around on camera, either in stop action or with motion blur! (Would that be chaos instead??) A few things to pick up on, and these are just somewhat minor, would be to get the camera directly overhead of the game to avoid the perspective lines... Also some color would add a bit more to the image! You are definitely thinking outside the box!', '2010-07-13 21:13:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091549, 895127, 10785, '<td valign="top">I like the use of lines in your composition to show order. You really framed it well with a nice evenly spaced V shape flowing through the image and that real straight line of markers up the center! Nice patterns! I think the B&amp;W conversion needs a little more umph. It has a lot of mid-tones, or greys but needs more highlight and shadows (whites and blacks) to give it that pop! Use the light during the golden hours to show shadows and give the image some depth. Overall good job!</td>', 'I like the use of lines in your composition to show order. You really framed it well with a nice evenly spaced V shape flowing through the image and that real straight line of markers up the center! Nice patterns! I think the B&W conversion needs a little more umph. It has a lot of mid-tones, or greys but needs more highlight and shadows (whites and blacks) to give it that pop! Use the light during the golden hours to show shadows and give the image some depth. Overall good job!', '2010-07-13 21:17:17.000000', NULL, 1),
