(6091975, 896048, 110473, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the positive comments on this picture for those who tried to understand what order I saw in the image. Obviously a lot of people cried shoehorn on this one and killed the score. The image ended up with more 10 votes and was favorited more then the winner so I am taking some consolation that this image was the best for this challenge in some people eyes which was a first for me since I''ve joined dp.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-07-14 02:54:19.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all the positive comments on this picture for those who tried to understand what order I saw in the image. Obviously a lot of people cried shoehorn on this one and killed the score. The image ended up with more 10 votes and was favorited more then the winner so I am taking some consolation that this image was the best for this challenge in some people eyes which was a first for me since I''ve joined dp.', '2010-07-14 02:01:44.000000', '2010-07-14 03:54:19.000000', 0),
(6092017, 895505, 64568, '<td valign="top">Thx guys, finally broke a 6 :)</td>', 'Thx guys, finally broke a 6 :)', '2010-07-14 02:32:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092033, 895874, 30861, '<td valign="top">LOL. So THAT was yours!!?<br/> <br/>I''m one of your 7''s. I have a soft spot for order-in-chaos (or is that chaos-in-order?) You actually beat my "Buoys on the Clamshack Wall", which was my gesture in the same conceptual direction...</td>', 'LOL. So THAT was yours!!? I''m one of your 7''s. I have a soft spot for order-in-chaos (or is that chaos-in-order?) You actually beat my "Buoys on the Clamshack Wall", which was my gesture in the same conceptual direction...', '2010-07-14 02:48:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092054, 895832, 62357, '<td valign="top">Thought for sure this would have scored higher.  But fabulous creative take on this challenge.  In my opinion one of the best!</td>', 'Thought for sure this would have scored higher.  But fabulous creative take on this challenge.  In my opinion one of the best!', '2010-07-14 03:03:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092057, 896048, 83313, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by techgeek360:</b></div><hr/><i> The image ended up with more 10 votes and was favorited then the winner so I am taking some consolation that this image was the best for this challenge in some people eyes which was a first for me since I''ve joined dp. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Averages are just that, averages. Like yourself, I also gauge the success of an entry on many more factors than the average vote received.</td>', 'Originally posted by techgeek360: The image ended up with more 10 votes and was favorited then the winner so I am taking some consolation that this image was the best for this challenge in some people eyes which was a first for me since I''ve joined dp.  Averages are just that, averages. Like yourself, I also gauge the success of an entry on many more factors than the average vote received.', '2010-07-14 03:09:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092059, 896136, 1031, '<td valign="top">I better study more of your entries more carefully -- I am virtually certain had <u>I</u> submitted this picture to the "Order" challenge it would have scored a point lower ... great colors and shapes!</td>', 'I better study more of your entries more carefully -- I am virtually certain had I submitted this picture to the "Order" challenge it would have scored a point lower ... great colors and shapes!', '2010-07-14 03:11:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092060, 896258, 62357, '<td valign="top">Prash, this is a really nice image.  The negative space works well.  The lighting is a bit flat and is not really giving enough detail in the feather.  It just does not stand out very well.  Trouble is, I think if you tried (in basic editing) to bring out the highlights better, you would end up blowing out the better lit part of the feather.<br/> <br/>I think in terms of this specific challenge it is just a little bit too outside the box and could easily be interpreted as DNMC.  I personally do not think so, but can see that others more rigid in their definition may.  Got a 6 from me and that would have been higher if the lighting on the feather was a little better.  Loved the negative space, although I wonder how it would have worked if the feather was on the right of the frame instead of the left?<br/> <br/>As we in the Western world read left to right, you often find that placing the main subject closer to the right of the frame works better than placing it on the left.  At least that is what I have been told by someone more experienced than myself!  It''s probably a subconscious thing and something I''d like to test one day.<br/> <br/>I would be disappointed with a 5.0 score for this to be honest.  I think it deserves a mid 5 score at least.  Sorry it didn''t do better.  If you want to post the original in our pm thread, do it and we can re-edit it.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Prash, this is a really nice image.  The negative space works well.  The lighting is a bit flat and is not really giving enough detail in the feather.  It just does not stand out very well.  Trouble is, I think if you tried (in basic editing) to bring out the highlights better, you would end up blowing out the better lit part of the feather. I think in terms of this specific challenge it is just a little bit too outside the box and could easily be interpreted as DNMC.  I personally do not think so, but can see that others more rigid in their definition may.  Got a 6 from me and that would have been higher if the lighting on the feather was a little better.  Loved the negative space, although I wonder how it would have worked if the feather was on the right of the frame instead of the left? As we in the Western world read left to right, you often find that placing the main subject closer to the right of the frame works better than placing it on the left.  At least that is what I have been told by someone more experienced than myself!  It''s probably a subconscious thing and something I''d like to test one day. I would be disappointed with a 5.0 score for this to be honest.  I think it deserves a mid 5 score at least.  Sorry it didn''t do better.  If you want to post the original in our pm thread, do it and we can re-edit it. ', '2010-07-14 03:12:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092061, 896152, 56545, '<td valign="top">thanks for the votes... the box on the right is a puzzle box with the picture of the drawer before I sorted it. It didn''t really come out with the low resolution, and I later thought that I should have made it larger. Oh well, at least I was able to finally clean out the junk drawer and complete a photo for the challenge at the same time :)</td>', 'thanks for the votes... the box on the right is a puzzle box with the picture of the drawer before I sorted it. It didn''t really come out with the low resolution, and I later thought that I should have made it larger. Oh well, at least I was able to finally clean out the junk drawer and complete a photo for the challenge at the same time :)', '2010-07-14 03:15:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092119, 896136, 103032, '<td valign="top">Harsh comments and Avg score of commenters.  Personally, I liked the vertical alignment and the "order" of the buoys.  Maybe a tighter crop (leaving out the window) would have helped.</td>', 'Harsh comments and Avg score of commenters.  Personally, I liked the vertical alignment and the "order" of the buoys.  Maybe a tighter crop (leaving out the window) would have helped.', '2010-07-14 04:42:36.000000', NULL, 0),
