(6092593, 895729, 73575, '<td valign="top">Placing the letters in "chaos" around "order" would have made for a nice visual pun - I half expected to see that... :(</td>', 'Placing the letters in "chaos" around "order" would have made for a nice visual pun - I half expected to see that... :(', '2010-07-14 12:11:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092607, 896056, 112739, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ThatChickOverThere:</b></div><hr/><i> Gee - a flower photo shoehorned into a challenge....never seen that before.  Seriously - we should save the flower shots for the flower or nature challenges.  I hate when people add a title to make you think that they visualized this photo as being for this challenge beforehand.  It is obvious that you just picked a photo you took this week and it has nothing to do with the theme at all.  Wastes voter time. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>One should never hate, "Thatchickoverthere". Really does terrible things to the universe. Try instead, to see the view from another''s POV. Put someone else''s shoes on for a bit. Con-structive works better than de-structive. What do you have left if everything is destructed? Chaos I''m afraid.</td>', 'Originally posted by ThatChickOverThere: Gee - a flower photo shoehorned into a challenge....never seen that before.  Seriously - we should save the flower shots for the flower or nature challenges.  I hate when people add a title to make you think that they visualized this photo as being for this challenge beforehand.  It is obvious that you just picked a photo you took this week and it has nothing to do with the theme at all.  Wastes voter time.   One should never hate, "Thatchickoverthere". Really does terrible things to the universe. Try instead, to see the view from another''s POV. Put someone else''s shoes on for a bit. Con-structive works better than de-structive. What do you have left if everything is destructed? Chaos I''m afraid.', '2010-07-14 12:19:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092677, 896249, 117285, '<td valign="top">There was just something about this image that said mycelium to me.  Glad to see my senses are sharp.  There is something about the appeal of this image that goes beyond easy description.  Is it the even balance of tonality caused by the consistent contrast between shadow and highlights?  Is it the repetitive pattern disrupted by jagged edges? Is it the points of chaos amidst the order?</td>', 'There was just something about this image that said mycelium to me.  Glad to see my senses are sharp.  There is something about the appeal of this image that goes beyond easy description.  Is it the even balance of tonality caused by the consistent contrast between shadow and highlights?  Is it the repetitive pattern disrupted by jagged edges? Is it the points of chaos amidst the order?', '2010-07-14 13:03:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092700, 894696, 86447, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully done... all of it.  Congrats on your ribbon!</td>', 'Wonderfully done... all of it.  Congrats on your ribbon!', '2010-07-14 13:18:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092709, 896170, 38162, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ThatChickOverThere:</b></div><hr/><i> SHOE + HORN = SCORE OF "1" </i></td></tr></table> <br/>ASS+HOLE=ASSHOLE<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by ThatChickOverThere: SHOE + HORN = SCORE OF "1"  ASS+HOLE=ASSHOLE ', '2010-07-14 13:26:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6092716, 896170, 38162, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NiallOTuama:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m afraid I don''t get why this is in the order competition. <br/>I''ll keep it in mind before Wednesday next and might figure it out by then. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I can accept the critique of shoe horn - at least you were not a dickhead like the other clown.  I go to lots of live gigs; roadies set up the kit with precision (order!) to suit the musician.  in some cases of course the musician does his (in this case a "her") own set up.  this kit was ready for the gig (thus the title).  whatever ... if ya got to explain it ...</td>', 'Originally posted by NiallOTuama: I''m afraid I don''t get why this is in the order competition. I''ll keep it in mind before Wednesday next and might figure it out by then.   I can accept the critique of shoe horn - at least you were not a dickhead like the other clown.  I go to lots of live gigs; roadies set up the kit with precision (order!) to suit the musician.  in some cases of course the musician does his (in this case a "her") own set up.  this kit was ready for the gig (thus the title).  whatever ... if ya got to explain it ...', '2010-07-14 13:34:08.000000', NULL, 0),
